$240^{\circ}=180^{\circ}+60^{\circ}$, so the acute reference angle is $60^{\circ}$. In Q3, sine and cosine are negative; tangent is positive.

(a) $\begin{aligned}\sin 240^{\circ}&=-\sin 60^{\circ}\\&=-\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\end{aligned}$

(b) $\begin{aligned}\cos 240^{\circ}&=-\cos 60^{\circ}\\&=-\frac{1}{2}\end{aligned}$

(c) $\begin{aligned}\tan 240^{\circ}&=\tan 60^{\circ}\\&=\sqrt{3}\end{aligned}$

