$315^{\circ}=360^{\circ}-45^{\circ}$, so the acute reference angle is $45^{\circ}$. In Q4, cosine is positive; sine and tangent are negative.

(a) $\begin{aligned}\sin 315^{\circ}&=-\sin 45^{\circ}\\&=-\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\end{aligned}$

(b) $\begin{aligned}\cos 315^{\circ}&=\cos 45^{\circ}\\&=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\end{aligned}$

(c) $\begin{aligned}\tan 315^{\circ}&=-\tan 45^{\circ}\\&=-1\end{aligned}$

